glyLinkedList.assert","category":"alias","sourceLine":16},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:15:36923","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.debug","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.debug","category":"alias","sourceLine":15},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:113:36936","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.len","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.len","category":"function","sourceLine":113},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:25:36927","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node","category":"container","sourceLine":25},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:57:36931","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.countChildren","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.countChildren","category":"function","sourceLine":57},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:45:36930","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.findLast","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.findLast","category":"function","sourceLine":45},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:28:36928","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.insertAfter","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.insertAfter","category":"function","sourceLine":28},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:34:36929","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.removeNext","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.removeNext","category":"function","sourceLine":34},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:70:36932","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.reverse","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.reverse","category":"function","sourceLine":70},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:103:36935","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.popFirst","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.popFirst","category":"function","sourceLine":103},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:83:36933","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.prepend","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.prepend","category":"function","sourceLine":83},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:90:36934","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.remove","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.remove","category":"function","sourceLine":90},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:18:36926","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.SinglyLinkedList","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.SinglyLinkedList","category":"alias","sourceLine":18},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:14:36922","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.std","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.std","category":"alias","sourceLine":14},{"id":"std/SinglyLinkedList.zig:17:36925","name":"std.SinglyLinkedList.testing","anchor":"std.SinglyLinkedList.testing","category":"alias","sourceLine":17}],"html":"<div id=\"std.SinglyLinkedList\"></div>\n<p class=\"api-source\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><a href=\"#L1\">Source line 1</a></p>\n<div class=\"api-description\"><p>A singly-linked list is headed by a single forward pointer. The elements\nare singly-linked for minimum space and pointer manipulation overhead at\nthe expense of O(n) removal for arbitrary elements. New elements can be\nadded to the list after an existing element or at the head of the list.</p>\n<p>A singly-linked list may only be traversed in the forward direction.</p>\n<p>Singly-linked lists are useful under these conditions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ability to preallocate elements / requirement of infallibility for\ninsertion.</li>\n<li>Ability to allocate elements intrusively along with other data.</li>\n<li>Homogenous elements.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h4>Fields</h4><div class=\"api-fields\">\n<pre><code>first: ?*<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a> = <span class=\"tok-null\">null</span></code></pre><div class=\"fieldDocs\"></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"api-members\"><ul>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/#std\"><code>std</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/debug/#std.debug\"><code>debug</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/debug/#std.debug.assert\"><code>assert</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/testing/#std.testing\"><code>testing</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList\"><code>SinglyLinkedList</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\"><code>Node</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.prepend\"><code>prepend</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.remove\"><code>remove</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.popFirst\"><code>popFirst</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.len\"><code>len</code></a></li>\n</ul></div>\n<section class=\"api-entry\" id=\"std.SinglyLinkedList.assert\"><h3><code>std.SinglyLinkedList.assert</code></h3>\n<p class=\"api-kind\">alias</p>\n<p class=\"api-source\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><a href=\"#L16\">Source line 16</a></p>\n<p>Alias of <a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/debug/#std.debug.assert\"><code>std.debug.assert</code></a></p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"api-entry\" id=\"std.SinglyLinkedList.debug\"><h3><code>std.SinglyLinkedList.debug</code></h3>\n<p class=\"api-kind\">alias</p>\n<p class=\"api-source\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><a href=\"#L15\">Source line 15</a></p>\n<p>Alias of <a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/debug/#std.debug\"><code>std.debug</code></a></p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"api-entry\" id=\"std.SinglyLinkedList.len\"><h3><code>std.SinglyLinkedList.len</code></h3>\n<p class=\"api-kind\">function</p>\n<p class=\"api-source\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><a href=\"#L113\">Source line 113</a></p>\n<div class=\"api-description\"><p>Iterate over all nodes, returning the count.</p>\n<p>This operation is O(N). Consider tracking the length separately rather than\ncomputing it.</p>\n</div>\n<pre class=\"api-prototype\"><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">pub</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">fn</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">len</span>(list: <a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList\">SinglyLinkedList</a>) <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span></code></pre>\n<h4>Parameters</h4><div class=\"api-parameters\">\n<pre><code>list: <a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList\">SinglyLinkedList</a></code></pre>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"api-entry\" id=\"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\"><h3><code>std.SinglyLinkedList.Node</code></h3>\n<p class=\"api-kind\">container</p>\n<p class=\"api-source\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><a href=\"#L25\">Source line 25</a></p>\n<div class=\"api-description\"><p>This struct contains only a next pointer and not any data payload. The\nintended usage is to embed it intrusively into another data structure and\naccess the data with <code>@fieldParentPtr</code>.</p>\n</div>\n<h4>Fields</h4><div class=\"api-fields\">\n<pre><code>next: ?*<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a> = <span class=\"tok-null\">null</span></code></pre><div class=\"fieldDocs\"></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"api-members\"><ul>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.insertAfter\"><code>insertAfter</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.removeNext\"><code>removeNext</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.findLast\"><code>findLast</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.countChildren\"><code>countChildren</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.reverse\"><code>reverse</code></a></li>\n</ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"api-entry\" id=\"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.countChildren\"><h3><code>std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.countChildren</code></h3>\n<p class=\"api-kind\">function</p>\n<p class=\"api-source\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><a href=\"#L57\">Source line 57</a></p>\n<div class=\"api-description\"><p>Iterate over each next node, returning the count of all nodes except\nthe starting one.</p>\n<p>This operation is O(N). Instead of calling this function, consider\nusing a different data structure.</p>\n</div>\n<pre class=\"api-prototype\"><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">pub</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">fn</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">countChildren</span>(node: *<span class=\"tok-kw\">const</span> <a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a>) <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span></code></pre>\n<h4>Parameters</h4><div class=\"api-parameters\">\n<pre><code>node: *<span class=\"tok-kw\">const</span> <a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a></code></pre>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"api-entry\" id=\"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.findLast\"><h3><code>std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.findLast</code></h3>\n<p class=\"api-kind\">function</p>\n<p class=\"api-source\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><a href=\"#L45\">Source line 45</a></p>\n<div class=\"api-description\"><p>Iterate over the singly-linked list from this node, until the final\nnode is found.</p>\n<p>This operation is O(N). Instead of calling this function, consider\nusing a different data structure.</p>\n</div>\n<pre class=\"api-prototype\"><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">pub</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">fn</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">findLast</span>(node: *<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a>) *<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a></code></pre>\n<h4>Parameters</h4><div class=\"api-parameters\">\n<pre><code>node: *<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a></code></pre>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"api-entry\" id=\"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.insertAfter\"><h3><code>std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.insertAfter</code></h3>\n<p class=\"api-kind\">function</p>\n<p class=\"api-source\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><a href=\"#L28\">Source line 28</a></p>\n<pre class=\"api-prototype\"><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">pub</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">fn</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">insertAfter</span>(node: *<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a>, new_node: *<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a>) <span class=\"tok-type\">void</span></code></pre>\n<h4>Parameters</h4><div class=\"api-parameters\">\n<pre><code>node: *<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a></code></pre>\n<pre><code>new_node: *<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a></code></pre>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"api-entry\" id=\"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.removeNext\"><h3><code>std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.removeNext</code></h3>\n<p class=\"api-kind\">function</p>\n<p class=\"api-source\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><a href=\"#L34\">Source line 34</a></p>\n<div class=\"api-description\"><p>Remove the node after the one provided, returning it.</p>\n</div>\n<pre class=\"api-prototype\"><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">pub</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">fn</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">removeNext</span>(node: *<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a>) ?*<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a></code></pre>\n<h4>Parameters</h4><div class=\"api-parameters\">\n<pre><code>node: *<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a></code></pre>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"api-entry\" id=\"std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.reverse\"><h3><code>std.SinglyLinkedList.Node.reverse</code></h3>\n<p class=\"api-kind\">function</p>\n<p class=\"api-source\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><a href=\"#L70\">Source line 70</a></p>\n<div class=\"api-description\"><p>Reverse the list starting from this node in-place.</p>\n<p>This operation is O(N). Instead of calling this function, consider\nusing a different data structure.</p>\n</div>\n<pre class=\"api-prototype\"><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">pub</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">fn</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">reverse</span>(indirect: *?*<a href=\"/zig-docs/en/std/SinglyLinkedList/#std.SinglyLinkedList.Node\">Node</a>) <span 